  },
  "name": "Generate branded proposal PDFs from a brief with AI + ShipPDF (poll)",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "282fc5e3-dd3b-4b17-979b-f220e593f7ff",
      "name": "Overview",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -368,
        -256
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 480,
        "height": 896,
        "content": "# \ud83d\udea2 ShipPDF \u2014 AI proposals on autopilot\n\n![ShipPDF](https://shippdf.com/assets/boat-mascot.png)\n\nGenerate branded proposal PDFs from a brief with AI + ShipPDF.\n\n### How it works\n\nA proposal brief submitted through the form is structured by an Anthropic-powered Information Extractor, then sent to ShipPDF to render a branded PDF from your own template. The workflow **polls** ShipPDF every few seconds until generation finishes, then branches on the result: a completed PDF is downloaded, emailed via Gmail, and archived to Google Drive; a failed one is routed to a placeholder alert. Polling means it runs on any n8n \u2014 Cloud or self-hosted \u2014 with no public callback URL.\n\n### Setup steps\n\n- Add a **ShipPDF API** credential (HTTP Bearer Auth, your key with `documents:create` + `documents:read`) and select it on both **Post Document to ShipPDF** and **Poll ShipPDF for Result**.\n- Add **Anthropic** credentials for the chat model and verify the extraction attributes match your ShipPDF template's data schema.\n- In **Post Document to ShipPDF**, set your `template_id` and map the `data` fields.\n- Connect **Gmail** and **Google Drive** credentials and set the recipient, subject, body, and archive folder.\n- Replace the failure placeholder with a real alert (Slack, email, ticket).\n\n### Notes\n\n- **Credits:** one ShipPDF credit per generated PDF. The `Idempotency-Key` **header** makes retries safe \u2014 a replay returns the original document, no double charge.\n- **Any model:** ships with Claude Sonnet 4.6; swap the chat model for ChatGPT (OpenAI), Gemini, Mistral, or local Ollama \u2014 the Information Extractor accepts any.\n- **Failures:** invalid data is rejected at the generate step with HTTP 422 before any credit; render/billing failures arrive as `status: failed` on the poll.\n\n### Customization\n\nCustomize the extraction schema, ShipPDF template/branding, email copy, Drive folder, and failure handling to fit different proposal types or sales processes.\n\nFree ShipPDF API key \u2192 https://shippdf.com"
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "1c4aa93e-791e-41bf-ba15-c4eb5017d589",
      "name": "Section: capture",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        192,
        80
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 240,
        "height": 320,
        "content": "## Capture proposal brief\n\nStarts the workflow when a user submits a new proposal brief through the form."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "78a855bf-633a-409a-86d5-9068e2c743a6",
